  "id": "implicit-memory",
  "term": "implicit memory",
  "definition": "Implicit memory is memory or learning that operates without conscious awareness, shown in the way cognitive processing adapts to incoming information without deliberate recall. It is commonly contrasted with explicit memory, which involves conscious remembering, although the two may partly overlap.",
